-- The planner's estimate of what Phase A keeps travels with the plan, and
-- a multi-stage predicate whose Phase A keeps several times that falls back
-- before emitting a row. d % 2 = 0 has no statistics and is estimated at
-- 0.5% whatever it keeps, so it leads Phase A; it really keeps half the
-- rows, and every segment falls back. (It can fail -- integer modulo -- so
-- it may lead only from the front of the qual: s + 0 = 1 rather than s = 1
-- keeps it there, being as costly, and is the same 90%.) The misled orders
-- above keep 3% against a planted 0.1% and stay under twice the gate, so
-- they do not.
SELECT gio_stages('SELECT c FROM gp_ord WHERE d % 2 = 0 AND s + 0 = 1') AS expression_leads;
